theme_override_font_sizes/font_size = 22
text = "There had been more to Pinktunes making rather than just for moonshot. My slight interest in the 
game world, specifically through godot, had begun earlier. Back in the end of september, I participated 
in a game jam with friends, which was one of which Hackclub was hosting globally; Daydream! In my 
city here in Vancouver, the event was hosted by BCYDC, the largest hack club organization in all of 
British Columbia. My friends and I had spent the entire day experimenting with the godot engine, and 
by the end, we had contructed a functioning mini game from start to finish. From then on, I had been 
inspired to work forward on new games as well! When I heard about moonshot, I was all in. My effort
eventually lead me to the creation of Pinktune!


I hadnt coded much in my youth, it was infact my friends who got me into it as they had been doing it 
before and had participated in other hackclub events. I learned very basic code in school, programming 
on scratch. Later, I learned to use HTML to make a website and eventually, Godot to make my own games"

